[39.982413, "o", "    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 13 tool call(s) so far\r\n  [tools] 13 call(s) without changing a file — nudging to decide\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 13 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ The problem is clear: the `pip` module files are missing from `/usr/local…\r\n  │ I'll restore pip using `ensurepip`:\r\n[approval] bash: python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 14 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ It says \"already satisfied\" but the module is missing. Let me force reins…\r\n[approval] bash: python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade --default-pip 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade --default-pip 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 15 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip 2>&1\r\n    ✗ bash — exit 2\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 16 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ `ensurepip` thinks pip i"]
[39.982457, "o", "s already installed because the `.dist-info` is t…\r\n[approval] bash: rm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info && python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade --default-pip 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash rm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info &&…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 17 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ Now let me verify it works:\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 --version && python3 -m pip --version — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 --version && python3 -m pip --version\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 18 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 install --dry-run requests 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 install --dry-run requests 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 19 tool call(s) so far\r\npip is fully working again.\r\n\r\n**What was wrong:** The `pip` package files had been deleted from `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/`, but the stale `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` metadata directory was left behind. This caused `ensurepip` to believe p"]
[39.982471, "o", "ip was already installed and skip the reinstall.\r\n\r\n**Fix:** Removed the stale `.dist-info` directory, then ran `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade --default-pip` to restore pip from the bundled wheel. Both `pip3` and `python3 -m pip` are now functional.\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=qwen3.6-35b tools=19 surface=48cd0ade3676\r\n"]
